-- CK-86: Elm's `exposing (Box(..))` for a type whose constructor has the
-- type's own name. The hint (CK-47's, R1) lists the type and then every
-- constructor, so it suggests `exposing (Box, Box)` — and that suggestion is
-- itself refused, as DUPLICATE EXPOSED NAME. The form that works is
-- `exposing (Box)`, which exposes the type and its same-named constructor
-- (`language.md` §5.2). Expected: the one diagnostic, suggesting
-- `exposing (Box)` and never `Box, Box`.
pub type Box
    = Box Int
